The package ggml provides CMake integration:

  find_package(ggml CONFIG REQUIRED)
  target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE ggml::ggml)

Available vcpkg features:
  metal  - Metal GPU backend (macOS/iOS, auto-enabled on Apple)
  vulkan - Vulkan GPU backend
  cuda   - CUDA GPU backend
  opencl - OpenCL GPU backend
  hexagon - Experimental Hexagon HTP backend (Android ARM64, opt-in)

Hexagon builds use a locally installed official Qualcomm SDK/compiler. Set
HEXAGON_SDK_ROOT and HEXAGON_TOOLS_ROOT, and forward both through the triplet's
VCPKG_ENV_PASSTHROUGH. The port does not download the SDK. It builds and installs
libggml-htp-v73/v75/v79/v81.so alongside the Android backend; consumers must stage
the skeletons and make their directory available to FastRPC via DSP_LIBRARY_PATH
before backend enumeration. Use the same build for host backend and DSP skeletons.

The SDK and runtime artifacts are for authorized internal evaluation; enabling
this feature does not establish redistribution rights.
